Z||000000||Flamberge||10-18-2001||06:27 PM||||I posted in the tech forum about getting orthogonal views of a Fiero, but no one knew where to find any, so I decided to wing it and build one anyway based on pictures. <P>This is a jpeg of a 3d studio max file I made last night. It isn't finished, and is based on the 89 Fiero, not the fastback production cars. (Once the prototype of the...uh...prototype is finished, I will move on to the production model(s) starting with the 88GT. (Gee I wonder why.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Keep in mind that I am a student though, so it might not look as good as real life, and I have thrown a little artistic lisence in there as well. Comments/ways I can improve it? I haven't done the rear view mirrors, glass surfaces, tail lights, bumber shape, b-piller glass, etc. But the overall shape is there, as is some temporary all-purpose rims.<P>Thanks. (and sorry for the size)<P> <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/firstpic.jpg"> <P>If the code doesn't work, and the pic doesn't show, the URL is <BR> <A HREF="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/firstpic.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://flamberge.iwarp.com/firstpic.jpg</A> <P>(Edited by Cliff Pennock so the picture would show up)<P><BR>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||7
