Z||000003||loafer87gt||10-18-2001||07:05 PM||||How did you go about modeling the car? Did you loft the shape or use NURBS? Looks good, can't wait to see the Fastback model. If you are interested, we could work on a joint 3D max model. I was going to create a 3d model of the interior of the car based on my 87 GT. It would be cool to pair up with your exterior model. Drop me a line at loafer@shaw.ca if your interested.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Flamberge||10-18-2001||07:16 PM||||Thanks all. =) I actually just used a 89 side view in the viewport background, then vertex edited a box that had 20x20x20 and after I got it the shape I wanted, started extruding faces, shapemerging lines, and then meshsmoothed the whole thing. <P>I'll email you, a joint project sounds great, though I am just a student, and have only been dabbling with max since 3.1. (about 9 months.)<P>(And thanks to the admin for fixing the pic.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000005||Cheever3000||10-18-2001||07:25 PM||||That rocks!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||08:20 PM||||Great start... I had to make a vehicle for my "Max" class in school- went with an antique beater pickup instead of the car- easier to fake stuff where I needed it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Keep up the good work- I have often thought about how cool it would be to have a 3D Fiero Model for Max, I just don't have the time or patience for long-term projects. Again- Keep up the good work!||||reg||1
Z||000007||hobbitt||10-18-2001||09:41 PM||||i'd love to get my hand on that file!!!looks great so far!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Flamberge||10-19-2001||02:48 AM||||I am pretty happy with it, and will keep posting pics as I go along. I am thinking that if the finished model looks good, I could start toying with the idea of "cloning" people's rides here and giving them the pics... I need the practice, and some of the fieros I have seen here are quite nice. (I particularly like Fiero Lisa's ride and NOS3800 (?) and his custom intakes...of what I have seen, but there are too many to name. Once I get the basic shape accurate, it won't be difficult making templates for the nose cone, fast/notchback, etc... <P>would people be willing to send me really nice front/side/back views of their rides? (The images have to be as close to flat as possible, like the white Fiero in the top frame.<P>flamberge01@hotmail.com<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||10
